# Pre-Upload GCS Validation

## SCHEMA PLACEMENT

RULE MOVED: See `imports/service-domain-schema-in-uic.mdc` for domain schema placement rules.
See `imports/no-schema-outside-contracts.mdc` for the master "no schema outside UAC or UIC" enforcement rule.

SUMMARY: Domain data contracts (Pydantic BaseModel, TypedDict, @dataclass) belong in UIC `domain/<service-name>/`.
The ONLY schema that stays in a service is `SchemaDefinition` / `ColumnSchema` — these are parquet write enforcement
descriptors (infrastructure), not data contracts.

## PRE-UPLOAD VALIDATION (unchanged, still required)

RULE: Call `validate_timestamp_date_alignment()` before every GCS write.
WHY: Misaligned timestamps cause partition read failures; schema drift causes silent corruption.

  from unified_domain_client import validate_timestamp_date_alignment
  validate_timestamp_date_alignment(df, date=processing_date)  # before every write

## DO:
  # SchemaDefinition: stays in service (infrastructure only)
  # schemas/output_schemas.py
  MY_OUTPUT_SCHEMA = SchemaDefinition(name="my_output", version="1.0", ...)

  # Pre-upload: always validate before write
  validate_timestamp_date_alignment(df, date=date)
  writer.write(df)  # only after validation passes

## NEVER:
  Write to GCS without calling validate_timestamp_date_alignment first
  Put cross-repo Pydantic/TypedDict contracts in service `schemas/output_schemas.py` (that file is for SchemaDefinition only)
  # For schema placement violations: see imports/service-domain-schema-in-uic.mdc
